  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 11,
  "Question": "The length of the interval of solutions of the inequality \\[a \\le 2x + 3 \\le b\\] is \\(10.\\) What is \\(b - a?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\)",
    "B": "\\(10\\)",
    "C": "\\(15\\)",
    "D": "\\(20\\)",
    "E": "\\(30\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "To find the interval's length, first isolate \\(x\\). Subtracting \\(3\\) from all three parts and dividing by the positive number \\(2\\) preserves both inequality directions:\n\\[\n\\frac{a-3}{2}\\le x\\le\\frac{b-3}{2}.\n\\]\nThe interval has positive length, so its upper endpoint exceeds its lower endpoint. Its length is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{b-3}{2}-\\frac{a-3}{2}\n=\\frac{b-a}{2}=10.\n\\]\nMultiplying by \\(2\\) gives \\(b-a=20\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
